<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-004-AL9>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-004-AL9" ;
  triage:title "AL.9 graft outbound write physical-proof row still 'static/source proof' only, not runtime evidence" ;
  triage:description "Physical proof matrix's atm-graft-write and CLI activation rows were backed only by source/static inspection, not by runtime execution producing recorded transcript/log. INDEPENDENT REVIEW (quality-mgr, 2026-08-10, integrate/phase-al@fc73d4ec / PR #824): verified via gh pr diff that PR #824 (docs-only, AL9-physical-proof-matrix.md +3/-3, sprint-AL9-physical-proof-ledger-freeze.md +23/-0) changes the CLI local write and graft outbound write rows' disposition text to 'Static/source proof; final-candidate runtime row pending', naming team-lead as owner and the frozen final integrate/phase-al candidate SHA as trigger. This resolved the unowned/unscheduled aspect of the gap but did not close the finding at that time. SECOND INDEPENDENT REVIEW (quality-mgr, 2026-08-10, develop@1e82cd3c3a0fbbd8471d426aea30787dbb979887): the CLI-local-write occurrence (AL9-doc-gap-1) is now closed. Verified directly: site/reports/smoke/macos/rand-m5.local/20260808T191357786414Z-pid23030-localhost/ and .../20260808T191410895708Z-pid23245-local-ip/ are committed on develop at 1e82cd3c3, and each report's case JSON (localhost.json, local-ip.json) contains 10 full attempt cycles of doctor/send/read/requires-ack/acknowledgement-reply PASS results with distinct real ULID message IDs -- genuine repeated runtime-executed atm send/read/ack transcripts, not static claims. Independently confirmed these exercise the atm-http-runtime path, not the frozen legacy daemon: crates/atm/src/composition.rs:491 and crates/atm-graft/src/lib.rs:266 both wire async_transport via atm_http_runtime::preferred_local_client(...), whose HttpRuntimeClient::execute (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/client.rs) POSTs to /v1/atm/messages (asserted at crates/atm-http-runtime/src/client.rs:809). CLI local write is closed on this evidence. The graft-outbound-write occurrence (AL9-doc-gap-2) remains open and is now the sole remaining scope of this finding: per team-lead's own check, `just smoke graft-hermes` has never been run and zero graft-hermes artifacts exist under site/reports/ on develop. Per the user's standing constraint ('we are not running another smoke-test until final integration -> develop review occurs'), no new smoke test may be executed right now to close AL9-doc-gap-2; it stays open, gated to the same final evidence-pass window as ATM-QA-002-AL9's M5 row. Windows<->M4 (AL.14/15) is a separately tracked, unaffected item." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-al" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
